In the exterior basis
$(s_1,\ldots,s_6)=(\delta a,\delta b,\delta d,ab,ad,bd)$,
put ${\mathsf E}_i=\bigwedge^2 A_i-I$. The combined relation image is
$\mathbb Z\langle s_1,s_2,s_5,s_6,s_3+6s_4\rangle$.
The reverse inclusion is witnessed by
\[
 \begin{aligned}
 s_1&={\mathsf E}_0s_4,& s_2&={\mathsf E}_1s_4,\\
 s_5&=2{\mathsf E}_0s_1-2{\mathsf E}_0s_2+{\mathsf E}_0s_4-{\mathsf E}_0s_5-{\mathsf E}_1s_6,\\
 s_6&=-2{\mathsf E}_0s_1+2{\mathsf E}_0s_2+{\mathsf E}_0s_4+{\mathsf E}_0s_5-{\mathsf E}_0s_6+{\mathsf E}_1s_6,\\
 s_3+6s_4&=-5{\mathsf E}_0s_1+9{\mathsf E}_0s_2+2{\mathsf E}_0s_5-{\mathsf E}_0s_6+3{\mathsf E}_1s_6.
 \end{aligned}
\]
The functional
$\xi=a^\vee\wedge b^\vee+6d^\vee\wedge\delta^\vee$
annihilates every relation, has exactly this kernel, and evaluates
to one on $s_4$. Hence the fibre term is
$\mathbb Zs$, with $s=[a\wedge b]$ and quotient coordinate $\xi$.


All thirteen exterior-matrix occurrences use their defined matrix symbol.
Correction to the informational wording above: nineteen occurrences (one definition and eighteen formula uses); the mathematical substitution and assertion are unchanged.
